    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391">

                <pb facs="0557" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg483"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Coggeshall.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-12-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 5, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatches Nos. 13 and 14 have been
                    received. In your No. 14 you gave me an account of the agitation in diplomatic
                    circles of complaints of the United States of Colombia against Ecuador.</p>
                <p>You inform me that speculations concerning a movement for the free navigation of
                    the Amazon are connected with those rumors. I shall hold myself under obligation
                    for such other information as you can give me on that interesting subject.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. T. Coggeshall,</hi> Esq., &amp;<hi
                            rendition="#italic">c</hi>., <hi rendition="#italic">Quito.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
